0,Luri music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luri_music,"The most popular Luri musical instruments include sorna, Karna, dohol, tâl (Luri kamancheh), [3] tonbak (tomak), and the common Iranian traditional instruments. Meanwhile, the Luri kamancheh is the only one that is fundamentally different from other Iranian music instruments. [4] The Lurs select the Mâhur as their basic musical scale to showcase the magnificence, grandeur and independence of ...","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
1,Lurs - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lurs,"Luri is a Western Iranian language continuum spoken by about four million people. The continuum constitutes the three dialects of Bakhtiari, Luristani and Southern Luri which linguist Anonby situates between Kurdish and Persian. [7]","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
2,Luri Folk Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/luri-folk-music,"Luri folk music is the traditional music of the Lur (Luri/Lak/Bakhtiari) peoples of Iran's Zagros Mountains. It is a living, orally transmitted art that intertwines pastoral life, epic storytelling, and communal dance.","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
3,Luri Music - theinfolist.com,https://www.theinfolist.com/html/ALL/l/L/Luri_music.html,"Luri (, ) is a Southwestern Iranian language continuum spoken by the Lurs, an Iranian people native to West Asia. The Luri dialects are descended from Middle Persian and are Central Luri, Bakhtiari,G. R. Fazel, 'Lur', in Muslim Peoples: A World Ethnographic Survey, ed. R. V. Weekes (Westport, 1984), pp. 446-447 and Southern Luri.","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
4,IRANIAN: PERSIAN & SOUTHERN LURI - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e1VnsFZgjAk,"Southern Luri speakers belong predominantly to the Lur ethnic group, who have a rich cultural heritage that includes traditional music, dance, and oral storytelling.","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
5,Lur Tribal Music: Sounds Of Western Iran's Heritage,https://nativetribes.blog/blog/lur-tribal-music-sounds-of,"Unveiling the Essence of Lur Tribal Music Okay, so what exactly is Lur tribal music? Well, at its heart, it's the folk music of the Lur people, an Iranian ethnic group primarily residing in the Zagros Mountains of Western Iran. This music isn't just about entertainment, guys; it's a living, breathing part of their culture. It's played at weddings, celebrations, mourning ceremonies, and even ...","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
6,Luristan لرستان - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zgodD2fomvk,"Luristan is a quite big land located in Zagros Mountains , the big part of Luristan is In Iran and the smaller one in Iraq . Lur people have their Own language,music,dance,culture,clothes and so on.","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
7,Persia Reference: Luri Music,https://persiareference.blogspot.com/2011/05/luri-music.html,"The Lurs constitute part of the Southwestern branch of the Iranian peoples and part of the Indo-Iranian linguistic group, spread across the Iranian plateau, stretching from the Hindu Kush to central Anatolia and from Central Asia to the Persian Gulf - a region that is sometimes termed Greater Iran.","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
8,Luri music - Wikipedia,https://wiki.privacytools.io/wiki/Luri_music,"Music instruments The most popular Luri musical instruments include sorna, Karna, dohol, tâl (Luri kamancheh), 3 tonbak (tomak), and the common Iranian traditional instruments. Meanwhile, the Luri kamancheh is the only one that is fundamentally different from other Iranian music instruments. 4 The Lurs select the Mâhur as their basic musical scale to showcase the magnificence, grandeur and ...","Luri, Southern",Indo-European
